      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Returning `null` when `budget.isCpuDeadlineExceeded()` at lines 408 and 420 makes `BoundedMarkdownWriter.finish()`\u0027s CPU check unreachable and causes `LeanHtml.tryRenderMarkdownSafeHtml` (lines 919-935) to treat CPU expiry as a normal Markdown fallback, rendering `\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e` and continuing for up to 63 more blocks instead of aborting immediately. Throw `OutputLimitExceeded.INSTANCE` at line 408 (and remove the duplicate `return null` check at lines 419-421 so `writer.finish()` throws directly), and also throw `OutputLimitExceeded.INSTANCE` in `LeanHtml.tryRenderMarkdownSafeHtml` if CPU expires when `tryConsumeMarkdown` returns `false`.",
