      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that PS 4 scans identifiers across all declaration bodies, signatures, imports, and directives, `0x1D00..0x1DBF` (excluding only `0x1D62..0x1D6A`) flags Unicode `MODIFIER_LETTER` superscripts (`0x1D2C..0x1D61` and `0x1D9B..0x1DBF`) used throughout standard Lean 4 and Mathlib notation (such as `sᶜ`, `Cᵒᵖ`, `Rᵐᵒᵖ`, `Aᵀ`, `Aᴴ`, and `Gᵃᵇ`), and standalone `ν` (U+03BD) and `ℓ` (U+2113) are also ubiquitous Mathlib variables. This triggers widespread false-positive `LeanTrojanBanner` alerts, per-declaration `homoglyph` badges, and loss of compact cards across thousands of legitimate `.lean` files. Please exclude `Character.getType(cp) \u003d\u003d Character.MODIFIER_LETTER` from the `0x1D00..0x1DBF` range, and avoid flagging standalone `ν` and `ℓ` unless mixed with Latin in the same identifier.",
