      "side": 1,
      "message": "`scanGuillemetHomoglyphs` reimplements Lean 4 lexing separately from `LeanLexer` and diverges in several ways: it lacks `InterpCmdState` (so guillemet homoglyphs inside `println!`, `dbg_trace`, and `throwError` interpolations are skipped as plain strings while `stripLeanCommentsAndStringsForHygiene` masks them), `isInterpPrefixAt` omits `!LeanLexer.hasIdentPartBefore` and hardcodes `s/m/f/v` instead of `LeanSyntax.LEAN_INTERP_STRING_PREFIXES`, block comments advance 2 chars instead of `LeanLexer.matchBlockCommentOpenerLen` (misclosing doc-comment openers followed immediately by `/`), interpolation depth silently stops at 64, and `matchRawClose` duplicates `LeanLexer.matchRawStringCloseAt`. Existing tests also only place guillemet homoglyphs in `decl.name()`, leaving `scanGuillemetHomoglyphs` unexercised. Please share lexing logic with `LeanLexer` and add `LeanHtmlSecurityTest` cases covering non-declaration guillemets in expressions, `s!` and `println!` interpolations, and comments/strings.",
