      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`exceedsMarkdownNestingLimit` has three bypasses that defeat the new Markdown DoS caps. First, a container-scoped fence like `\u003e ```\\n` or `- ```\\n` (or an indented list fence) sets `inFence \u003d true` and never clears it when the blockquote or list ends, skipping every nesting, heading, pipe, and delimiter check for the rest of a 128 KiB docstring. Second, `\u003e` opens a blockquote unconditionally in CommonMark without trailing whitespace or another `\u003e`, so `\"\u003e- \".repeat(2000)` exits `atLineStart` with depth 0 (staying under 8,192 AST nodes) and `\u003e# ...` skips ATX heading counting. Third, `leadingSpaces` is never reset after container markers (so `   \u003e # ...` and `\u003e \u003e \u003e \u003e # ...` fail `leadingSpaces \u003c\u003d 3`), Setext checks only charge `prevLineLen` rather than full paragraph length, and `isSetextHeadingUnderline` misses quoted underlines (`\u003e \u003d\u003d\u003d`), letting nested headings blow up `TocFormatter.setRoot` (which `MarkdownToHtml.renderToHtml` runs unconditionally). Please enter `inFence` only at top level (`lineQuoteOrListDepth \u003d\u003d 0` and `leadingSpaces \u003d\u003d 0`), handle `c \u003d\u003d \u0027\u003e\u0027` unconditionally while resetting `leadingSpaces \u003d 0` after container markers, and enforce heading count and total heading-text caps on the parsed AST in `LeanHtml.rewriteOpaqueMarkdownNodes` before rendering.",
